{"title":"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A right rectangular <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prism\" title=\"Prism\">prism</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3cb5ead6c0d867c737b26631bf322627c0621d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> (i.e., a rectangular parallelpiped) has sides of integral length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d02bb2275100261109b043261e702124460a83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb8e1b8da40f20391d89404f8326236a4433935c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\le b\\le c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />  A plane parallel to one of the faces of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3cb5ead6c0d867c737b26631bf322627c0621d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> cuts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3cb5ead6c0d867c737b26631bf322627c0621d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> into two prisms, one of which is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Similar\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Similar\">similar</a> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72372ce518e97b2d43a1f0bcafbdc88302ed9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> and both of which have nonzero volume.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a974a112474dfd23b131027c208edaf2b41bae87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1995,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> for how many ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> does such a plane exist?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the prism similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d534e199fa536c255a869fc05ba3afd636623de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le y \\le z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. Then \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83b589d1ce0653b46106e03a94b02113f71ff76c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{a} = \\frac{y}{b} = \\frac zc &lt; 1.\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"33\" /> \n</p><p>Note that if the ratio of similarity was equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we would have a prism with zero volume. As one face of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is a face of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> share at least two side lengths in common. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c2e2062561e320e9e95324760f782107765ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; a, y &lt; b, z &lt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />, it follows that the only possibility is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e908c970fb8d677df04faa2deb445396560bf801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a,z=b=1995$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" />. Then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/389a5f452bc42ca3834beb2a917ba7dc611acb10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{a} = \\frac{a}{1995} = \\frac{1995}{c} \\Longrightarrow ac = 1995^2 = 3^25^27^219^2.\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>The number of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/461fd3e698e3947eff6b436ddc37807a40671b40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^25^27^219^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9ab21c48271f5ba51da9cda9b591983c466d52aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2+1)(2+1)(2+1)(2+1) = 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" />. Only in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4765950aec003604bda6f959d921fe52bf2ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac {81}2 \\right\\rfloor = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"84\" height=\"43\" /> of these cases is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1ace77e32a7ea033fd53047e80344dcdfbf0da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"10\" /> (for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f717c40ef1d78faf6efbaef5c9e6f804d544faf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" />, we end with a prism of zero volume). We can easily verify that these will yield nondegenerate prisms, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2557a6bcfe619e164725d5dbf345040c75b7b53d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{040}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME\" title=\"1995 AIME\">1995 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017041534\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 215/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1770/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 92/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4879/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.016      1 -total\n 60.25%    8.444      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.16%    5.348      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2967:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017041534 and revision id 55036. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}